= The April Theses

On 16 April Lenin arrived in Petrograd in a sealed train that had crossed Germany. At the Finland Station he told the crowd that the revolution had not ended, and the next day he put out his "April Theses": no support for the Provisional Government, all power to the soviets, an end to the war, the confiscation of the landlords' estates.

Even most Bolsheviks thought the theses mad. Plekhanov called them "delirium". Many Bolsheviks in the provinces still work in joint committees with the Mensheviks, and Kamenev's wing hopes to remain on speaking terms with the other socialists.

- @dismiss: Dismiss the theses. This is anarchism, not Marxism.
- @unity: Invite Kamenev's wing to a unity conference.

@dismiss
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {bolshevik: 2, rel_bol: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 1);
!}

Sukhanov remarked that Lenin would be left alone, outside the revolution. This was an error: Lenin was outside the Soviet's consensus, and so was the whole population.

@unity
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 8, bolshevik: -3});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 6);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -2);
Q.bol_unity = 1;
!}

A unity conference was held with the local Bolsheviks in Tiflis, Moscow and a number of provincial towns. Lenin ignored the results. Kamenev's wing, pleased with the contact, has become more critical of him.
